Cure for Lempeck Hargrin	29	{"kind":"quest","title":"Cure for Lempeck Hargrin","wikiPath":"/Cure_for_Lempeck_Hargrin","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"North Qeynos","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Astaed Wemor","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[],"rewards":[{"text":"Shining Star of Light","item":"Shining Star of Light","wikiPath":"/Shining_Star_of_Light"}],"steps":[{"parts":["In ",{"title":"Rivervale"},", complete the ",{"title":"Honey Jum Quest"}," and receive ",{"title":"Honey Jum"},"."],"steps":[]},{"parts":["In ",{"title":"Qeynos","label":"North Qeynos"},", give the honey jum to ",{"title":"Astaed Wemor"}," and receive Prime Healer Potion [identifies as Potion of Disease Warding]."],"steps":[{"parts":["Note: you need good faction with ",{"title":"Astaed Wemor"}," or he will keep the honey jum and give nothing. (Warning: Amiable faction is required (wolf form seems to work). You will recieve dialogue for the quest down to apprehensive, but not dubious, but if you are indifferent or apprehensive, your Honey Jum will be eaten.)"],"steps":[]}]},{"parts":["In ",{"title":"West Karana"},", give the potion to ",{"title":"Lempeck Hargrin"}," and receive a LORE/NODROP Rusty Scythe. CAUTION: Sometimes he goes crazy and attacks you at this point. This is most likely related to the potion you give him. The potion that identifies as \"Potion of Disease Warding\" is the one you want. If it identifies as \"Ochre Potion Disease Ward\" or anything else, you'll get attacked."],"steps":[]},{"parts":["In ",{"title":"Qeynos","label":"North Qeynos"},", give the scythe to ",{"title":"Astaed Wemor"}," and receive ",{"title":"Shining Star of Light"},"."],"steps":[]}],"card":{"title":"Cure for Lempeck Hargrin","lines":["Minimum Level: 1 (Solo)","Classes: Cleric, Paladin","Related Zones: Rivervale, Misty Thicket, West Karana","Related NPCs: Kizzie Mintopp, Lempeck Hargrin"]},"links":["Qeynos","Astaed Wemor","Cleric","Paladin","Rivervale","Misty Thicket","West Karana","Kizzie Mintopp","Lempeck Hargrin","Shining Star of Light","Cleanse","Honey Jum Quest","Honey Jum","Prime Healer Potion","Priests of Life","Knights of Thunder","Guards of Qeynos","Bloodsabers","Antonius Bayle","Rusty Scythe","Whysia Flock"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Astaed Wemor","text":"Greetings. I am Astaed Wemor of the Paladins of the Temple of Life. We are the defenders of the all-giving Prime Healer. Are you [here to pray] or are you [here to assist the temple]?"},{"npc":"Astaed Wemor","text":"Good. There are a few in the congregation who require assistance. Will you be [traveling afar] or are you [staying close to Qeynos]?"},{"npc":"Astaed Wemor","text":"Then outfit yourself well. We will require you to visit Rivervale, the village of the halflings. There you shall find an herb merchant named Kizzie Mintopp. She has an ingredient we require. Tell her you are from the Temple of Life."},{"npc":"Astaed Wemor","text":"I pray to Rodcet Nife that you have made it back in time. Let's add a small amount of this honey jum to this and.. here is the potion. This potion must be taken to a sick member of the congregation. The man is Lempeck Hargrin. He lives in the west plains of Karana between the river and the crop fields. He is in dire need of this potion. He has an odd disease. We have tried everything to cure him and this is his last chance. Run to him."},{"npc":"Lempeck Hargrin","text":"Gree.. .. tings. How are you? Don't get too close to me. I have come down with something bad."},{"npc":"Lempeck Hargrin","text":"Thank you!! I felt the madness nearing my brain, but now I feel much better. Please take this as thanks - it is all I have to donate to Astaed Wemor. Be sure he gets it. I shall thank Rodcet Nife every day for sending help."},{"npc":"Astaed Wemor","text":"It is good to know that we saved Lempeck. He has given us his scythe as a donation to the temple. We shall find a use for it. As for your fine work at preserving the life of another, I reward you with the Shining Star of Life. Should you ever desire more strength in battle, call upon it to give you strength, but let it be known that at battle's end, you shall feel weaker than before you called upon the power. Just for a short time. When the power is drained, go to our temple storehouse and ask Whysia to [recharge the Shining Star of Life]. Go and serve life."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-10-27T05:12:35.148Z","outOfEra":false}
